Sat Nov 21 21:14:45 UTC 2026 - ahjolinna <ahjolinna@yahoo.com>

- Initial package, 0.1. Chat with Inkling 2 Mini from a Plasma 6
  panel widget, from the Assistant window (the widget in
  plasmawindowed), or from KRunner with "ai <question>", which answers
  in a notification with Copy and Continue in Assistant.
- Answers stream as Markdown with copyable code blocks. The model's
  thinking is shown, and a thinking effort setting goes to the chat
  template as reasoning_effort. Images and text files can be attached.
- The model can look up facts about the computer (read-only, fixed
  commands) and propose shell commands, which run only after the user
  presses Run, as the user, with a one-minute limit.
- A weather tool from Open-Meteo, for the place asked about, the
  settings' place, or the time zone's city.
- KRunner answers search the web when that is on, and use the lookups
  and the weather. The widget reloads its chat list when the service
  reports a change, so KRunner chats show up at once.
- Optional web search: DuckDuckGo's top 3 to 5 results go to the model,
  which cites them. When DuckDuckGo asks for a robot check, it falls
  back to the Instant Answer API for ten minutes.
- Saved chats with search, favorites, rename, duplicate, fork from an
  answer, delete, and export to Markdown, text or JSON. JSON imports.
- atropos-assistant-service, a D-Bus-activated Python service on the
  session bus, keeps the chats, runs the download, starts and stops the
  model, and serves KRunner.
- The widget sits on a panel or in the system tray.
- The widget downloads the model with progress, and starts it when the
  download finishes or the first message is sent. Setups from Light
  (UD-IQ1_S, 7.8 GB, the default) to Best (UD-Q8_K_XL, 22.9 GB) say
  whether they fit the computer's memory; Model Size… switches later.
  atropos-assistant-setup fetches llama.cpp b12613 (Vulkan) and
  Unsloth's Mainline_Support GGUF and checks their SHA-256 sums.
  b12613 includes PR #32704; builds without it print gibberish.
- The settings choose between Inkling 2 Mini on this computer and
  another OpenAI-compatible server. There is no Ollama setting:
  Ollama 0.40.17 runs inkling-2-mini on Apple silicon only.
- atropos-assistant.service runs llama-server on 127.0.0.1:18080 with
  --no-op-offload and a micro-batch sized to the free GPU memory. With
  op offload, llama.cpp stages the MoE experts on the GPU and needs a
  7 GiB compute buffer for this model, so it failed to load on 8 GB
  cards. A load error no longer restarts the service.
- llama-server leaves 2.5 GiB of graphics memory free (--fit-target,
  GPU_HEADROOM_MIB) and unloads after 15 idle minutes. With 0.7 GiB
  left on an 8 GB card, Spectacle failed with EGL_BAD_ALLOC and
  crashed.
